From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:48:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: an answer that wasn't streamed tells its pace
 (#5575)

Speed first orders keys by how fast they answered lately, but it kept
nothing from an answer that wasn't streamed: with no first token,
DecodeOf told nothing, noteSpeed kept nothing, and a pool whose callers
stream nothing had every key unmeasured for good -- Speed first went on
sending the first key in the list everything, which is what the
reporter saw (#5575). An unstreamed answer's pace is its output over
its whole wait, the reading the reporter gave the Requests page: kept
apart from a streamed one's average, which it would drag down (the
review of #5575), enough to order the seat by, weighed without a first
token. Fastest counts a told pace as measured, and the Routing page's
story says the whole-reply pace of a key first by it, where before it
said the key hadn't answered at all.
---
